  <!--=== Mod Setting related ===-->
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ModName>RimDark 40k - Framework - {0}</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ModName>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowRankTab>Always show Rank tab for player pawns. Will show even if no category or rank is available to the pawn</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowRankTab>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowCustomizationDebugOptions>Show decoration debug options when customizing armor</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowCustomizationDebugOptions>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationsPerRow>Decorations per row when customizing: {0}</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationsPerRow>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationsPerRowTooltip>Amount of decorations shown when applying decorations on things. Icons and texts can become small and overlap wierdly if too many decorations per row.</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationsPerRowTooltip>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ConfirmRankUnlock>Confirm rank unlock with popup. (Looking at you butterfingers)</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ConfirmRankUnlock>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationWorkEnabled>Fitting decorations and upgrades takes work</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationWorkEnabled>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationWorkEnabledTooltip>When on, accepting changes at a station sends the pawn to work for the combined work amount, and any upgrade costs are paid when the work finishes. When off, changes apply instantly and cost nothing.</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationWorkEnabledTooltip>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationCostEnabled>Fitting decorations and upgrades cost materials</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationCostEnabled>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationCostEnabledTooltip>When on, a decoration with a cost has to be paid for once per item before it can be fitted. When off, everything is free to fit and nothing is ever charged. Independent of the work setting. Anything fitted while this is off stays permanently unlocked on that item, so turning it back on will not re-lock it.</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.DecorationCostEnabledTooltip>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowDecorationsOnGround>Show decorations on unequipped armour and weapons</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowDecorationsOnGround>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowDecorationsOnGroundTooltip>Draws fitted decorations on items lying on the ground, on shelves or being carried. Only items on screen are drawn, so the cost is small; turn off if a very large armoury slows things down.</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.ShowDecorationsOnGroundTooltip>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AppearanceChangeWork>Work for a colour or texture change: {0}</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AppearanceChangeWork>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AppearanceChangeWorkTooltip>Flat work charged when an item's colours, masks or base texture change. Charged once per item, no matter how many things were recoloured on it.</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AppearanceChangeWorkTooltip>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.MinimumWork>Minimum work for any change: {0}</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.MinimumWork>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.MinimumWorkTooltip>No visit to the station takes less work than this, however small the change.</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.MinimumWorkTooltip>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.NotifyRankEligibility>Show a message when a pawn becomes eligible for a new rank</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.NotifyRankEligibility>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.NotifyGeneVariantAvailability>Show a message when a new gene variant becomes available to a pawn</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.NotifyGeneVariantAvailability>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AlwaysShowShields>Always show worn shields</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AlwaysShowShields>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AlwaysShowShieldsTooltip>When off, worn shields are only drawn while the wearer is drafted, fighting or was recently attacked.</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.AlwaysShowShieldsTooltip>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.RepairCostFactor>Repair cost: {0} of crafting cost for a full repair</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.RepairCostFactor>
  <BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.RepairCostFactorTooltip>How much of an item's crafting materials the repair station uses to restore it from no hit points to full. Repairs cost proportionally less the less damaged the item is.\n\nAt 0%, repairs are free.\n\nDefault: 50%</BEWH.Framework.ModSettings.RepairCostFactorTooltip>

